## Summary

**Approach:** LightGBM gradient boosting with native categorical handling, stratified 5-fold CV ROC AUC as the sole quality signal (test is unlabeled, so no leakage possible).

**Results:**
- Baseline LGBM (default-ish params + engineered features): 5-fold OOF AUC **0.94169**
- Optuna tuning (20 trials, 3-fold): best **0.94191** — only +0.0002, deemed noise; stopped tuning to save time
- CatBoost (same features): 3-fold OOF **0.9414** — rejected in favor of LGBM
- Final model retrained on full training data (iteration count from a 5% internal holdout, holdout AUC 0.9421), predictions on test

**Feature engineering:** charging station totals/ratio, income-per-car and income-per-commute-km, age×income, age/income bins, and categorical crosses (subsidy×home charging, subsidy×range anxiety). Strongest raw signals: `Subsidy_Available` (Yes: 27.5% vs No: 0.6% buy rate) and `Range_Anxiety_Level`.

**Deliverable:** `/work/submission.csv` — 286,571 rows, header `id,Will_Buy_EV`, ids identical to and in the same order as `/data/sample_submission.csv`, all values floats in [0,1] (mean 0.1747 ≈ base rate 0.1746), no nulls, no extra columns. Verified by direct comparison with the sample submission.

**Note:** `/work/.harness` is owned by another user and not writable in this session, so harness state (intent, world facts, decisions, evidence, AAR) was kept at `/work/.state/` instead. Total wall-clock used: ~60 minutes.
